   - MEN 2B is characterized by the presence of medullary thyroid carcinoma, pheochromocytomas, and mucosal neuromas. The patient's symptoms and findings align well with these conditions.

While MEN 2A also includes medullary thyroid carcinoma and hyperparathyroidism, the absence of hyperparathyroidism in this case and the emphasis on symptoms relating to catecholamines suggest MEN 2B is more fitting.

